{"moat":{"rating":"narrow","sources_of_moat":["Brand intangible asset: the largest athletic brand, with Nike, Jordan and Converse. Brand value is cited above $50B versus about $16B for Adidas.","Scale: FY26 revenue of $46.4B is almost twice Adidas's revenue. That gives Nike purchasing, sourcing and marketing leverage, plus athlete and team endorsement reach.","Performance product and innovation pipeline: Performance revenue is about $16B and grew high single digits in Q1 FY27 across running, football, basketball, tennis and golf.","Distribution breadth: sales in nearly 190 countries, owned stores plus wholesale, and the Nike app and SNKRS data. Nike is rebuilding wholesale partnerships."],"evidence":"The moat is real but weaker than it was. Consumer switching costs are negligible (cited by koalagains.com), so it rests almost entirely on brand and scale. Revenue fell from $51.4B in FY24 to $46.4B in FY26. EBIT margin fell from 12.7% to 8.3% and FCF margin from about 12.9% to about 4.7% (from the supplied filings summary). Euromonitor puts Nike's 2025 global sports-footwear share at 22.9%, down from 25.9%. Adidas rose from 11.7% to 12.2% (founderpin.com, citing Euromonitor). On, Hoka, New Balance and Asics are growing faster, though from much smaller bases. Management guides FY27 revenue down high single digits. Q1 FY27 Sportswear fell low double digits, Jordan fell mid-teens and Greater China fell 26%. Nike still has gross margin of about 43% and net cash, so the franchise is not broken. A wide moat is not supported by current results. Narrow is a judgment call.","industry_note":"unknown"},"management":{"rating":"average","capital_allocation":"Mixed. The ~$12.1B of buybacks to date were done at an average of about $97.57 a share, against a current price of about $34.61. Repurchases have been paused since Q1 FY26. FY26 dividends of $2,407M exceeded FCF of $2,184M, so the payout is not covered by FCF right now. Capex rose to $684M. The new Pace program costs about $1.0B in charges for about $2.5B of savings through FY31 (CNBC and the earnings-call summaries). Net cash is a plus: $8.4B of cash and short-term investments, with leverage of about 2x (Yahoo/GuruFocus call summary). Management has cut SG&A, with Q1 SG&A down 3%. It also admitted it underappreciated the need to split Sportswear into smaller consumer segments (TradingKey transcript summary). CEO Elliott Hill's 'Sport Offense' and the wholesale reset are showing results in Performance categories. The turnaround is taking longer than expected, and Denton (CFO) warned that the actions will weigh on results into FY28. A new CFO, David Denton, has just joined. Execution on the reset has not yet been shown.","governance_concerns":["Dual-class structure: Class A holders elect 8 of 11 directors and public Class B holders elect only 3 (Forbes, Stocktitan DEF 14A).","Control: Swoosh LLC (Phil Knight) owns 78.8% of Class A. Phil Knight owns another 9.8% and a Travis Knight trust owns 8.8% (Forbes). The Knight family holds about 97% of Class A, roughly 21% of total economic value (whoistheownerof.com).","A shareholder proposal for a dual-class sunset provision was filed by the New York City pension funds. Swoosh said it would vote against it and had no plans to implement it (Forbes). This leaves activism with little leverage.","Board independence: Travis Knight is not independent under NYSE rules, and Phil Knight is Chairman Emeritus with a standing observer invitation (DEF 14A).","Capital allocation and the long price decline, with about $12B of buybacks done at roughly three times today's price, remain open questions for public shareholders."]},"industry":{"growth_outlook":"Mixed. A third-party source cites global sportswear market growth of 7.2% in 2025 (sinofinetex.com, lower-quality). Nike's own FY27 revenue is guided to fall high single digits, with adjusted EPS of $1.15 to $1.35. Q1 FY27 Performance grew high single digits, but Sportswear, Jordan and China fell. Long-term industry growth beyond this is unknown.","competitive_intensity":"High and rising. Share is moving to running specialists and resurgent rivals. A third-party source (businessmodelanalyst.com) reports On grew about 30%, New Balance about 20%, Asics about 20%, Hoka 16% and Adidas 13%. Nike shrank 10% in its most recent full year. Adidas has regained lifestyle share through Samba and Gazelle. Local players such as Anta compete in China. Discounting is rising, and Q1 gross margin rose 60 bps despite higher discounts.","key_competitors":["Adidas","On Holding","Hoka (Deckers)","New Balance","Asics","Puma","Under Armour","Lululemon","Skechers","Anta Sports"]},"catalysts":["Growth in Performance categories (running, football, basketball, tennis, golf), which was up high single digits in Q1 FY27 and was $16B in FY26","Pace productivity program: about $2.5B of cumulative savings through FY31 against about $1.0B of charges","Stabilising Sportswear and Jordan, including the cut in Dunk supply of nearly 50%, and a cleaner wholesale channel","China marketplace reset. Management expects China to get worse for the balance of FY27 before it stabilises, so this is a later catalyst.","Reorganisation into three geographies (Americas, APGC, EMEA) from FY28, and a new campus in Bengaluru","Gross margin recovery: Q1 FY27 gross margin was 42.8%, up 60 bps","Possible resumption of buybacks (about $5.9B authorisation remains) once FCF recovers","Activism is a possible but difficult catalyst given the dual-class structure"],"citations":["https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/01/nike-nke-q1-2027-earnings.html","https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/nike-q1-earnings-call-highlights-000223968.html","https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/nike-inc-nke-q1-2027-050050135.html","https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/10/02/nike-nke-q1-2027-earnings-call-transcript/","https://ca.investing.com/news/company-news/nike-inc-nke-q1-2027-earnings-call-highlights-performance-gains-offset-by-china-reset-and--4863264","https://www.tradingkey.com/news/transcripts/262197031-tradingkey","https://wwd.com/footwear-news/shoe-industry-news/nike-running-basketball-training-growth-categories-q1-2027-1239306437/","https://founderpin.com/nike-vs-adidas-2026-which-sportswear-brand-leads/","https://businessmodelanalyst.com/nike-competitors-alternatives/","https://koalagains.com/stocks/NYSE/NKE/competition","https://www.companieshistory.com/nike-swot-analysis/","https://sinofinetex.com/nike-vs-adidas-2025-who-leads-global-sportswear-market/","https://www.forbes.com/sites/jimosman/2026/09/08/nike-stock-is-ripe-for-an-activist-but-theres-one-big-problem/","https://www.stocktitan.net/sec-filings/NKE/def-14a-nike-inc-definitive-proxy-statement-0e0f84e540fc.html","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0000320187/000032018726000089/nke-20260715.htm","https://whoistheownerof.com/who-is-the-owner-of-nike-2025-guide/"]}
